# Patterns to ignore when building chart packages.
.DS_Store
.git/
.gitignore
.bzr/
.bzrignore
.hg/
.hgignore
.svn/
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*~
.project
.idea/
*.tmproj
.vscode/

# Test suites and CI-only values. `helm package` packs everything not listed
# here, and the published client-1.9.107.tgz carried 41 helm-unittest suites
# plus ci/*-values.yaml -- 45 of its 96 entries, 39 % of its bytes. Nothing
# reads them from the tarball: `helm unittest ./client` and the ct/lint jobs
# run on the source checkout (helm-unittest's own README says to list `tests`
# here). scripts/check-chart-contents.sh refuses a packaged chart that carries
# either directory, so this rule is held by the artefact, not by this comment.
# LEADING SLASH, deliberately: Helm strips a trailing slash and then matches an
# unanchored name against EVERY path component, so a bare `tests/` would also
# drop a future `templates/tests/` hook directory (Helm's own `helm test`
# convention). `/tests/` anchors to the chart root -- measured: with `tests/`
# a `templates/tests/hook.yaml` vanished from the package; with `/tests/` it
# shipped and `tests/**` did not.
/tests/
/ci/
